 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pronouns after a preposition",
     "texto": [
      "After many prepositions, the stressed forms are used: **para mim** (for me), **para ti** (for you), **para ele/ela** (for him / her).",
      "With **com**, some forms are written as one word: **comigo** (with me), **contigo** (with you). Learn these forms within short expressions."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pronouns with the infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "With **vou**, **quero**, **posso** or **vais**, the pronoun goes **after** the infinitive: **vou visitá-lo** (I'm going to visit it), **quero comprá-la** (I want to buy it).",
      "When the infinitive ends in **-r**, the form is: **visitar** → **visitá-lo**, **comprar** → **comprá-la**, **fazer** → **fazê-lo**, **ver** → **vê-los**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Infinitive",
